      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, immediately rinse the wound under clean running water for at least five minutes while gently applying an antiseptic soap around (not deep inside) the injury. Do not attempt to \"seal\" the wound at home, as leaving it open cleaned with a simple bandage is the safest way to prevent deep infection from the rusty metal. Since you're unsure about the depth and potential exposure to *Clostridium tetani*, please plan to visit a healthcare provider as soon as your gardening project allows, as the standard protocol for rusty punctures is a tetanus booster shot.",
